peed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn11le07ob02re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to cut out"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to remove "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(phrasal verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: If I cut out all those things, what do I eat?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le07ob02aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to talk about beliefs and opinions."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "dairy"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "products containing or made from milk"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I removed all the sugar, fat, meat and dairy from my kitchen."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le07ob02aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "spice"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an aromatic or pungent vegetable substance used to flavor food"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There's nothing left except a few spices."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le07ob02aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to live on"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to depend on someone or something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(phrasal verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: If I had to live on what's in the fridge now, I would waste away to nothing."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le07ob02aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to waste away"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to lose energy and vigor; become enfeebled and weak"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(phrasal verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: If you don't eat, you will waste away."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le07ob02aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to throw together"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to quickly assemble"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I can help you with some meals that you can throw together that don't have any of the ingredients that you are trying to avoid."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le07ob02aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "vegan"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "without the use of animal products"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: If there were more demand, I would open a small vegan restaurant."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le07ob02aud07"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Other Ways of Talking about Result"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can talk about results or consequences of something by using a result clause in your sentences."}, {"type": "example", "content": "We were talking about the dangers of eating too much fat and sugar and, as a result, I've decided to do a cleanse."}, {"type": "text", "content": "There are several ways you can express a result. The following ways all use the word \u201cresult\u201d in them, but they are used in different ways.<br /> With these expressions, you should first provide the situation or action that led to the result, and then say what the result was after the expression."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Cause</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Result</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">There was a devastating earthquake in India yesterday, </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">and as a result</span>  thousands of people died.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">There was a devastating earthquake in India yesterday, </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\"> with the result that</span>  thousands of people died.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">There was a devastating earthquake in India yesterday.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\"> As a result</span> , thousands of people died.</span><br /><br />  If you want to begin a new sentence about the result, you can also use:<br /> <span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Consequently<br />  Therefore<br />  Thus<br />  For this/that reason</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">There was a devastating earthquake in India yesterday, </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\"> resulting in</span>  the deaths of thousands of people. </span><br /> <br /> (Notice the use of the noun \u201cdeath\u201d here instead of the verb \u201cdied\u201d as in the other sentences.)\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I removed all the sugar, fat, meat and dairy from my kitchen with the result that there's nothing left except a few spices."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Therefore, I can help you with some meals."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Long ago I worked in a vegan restaurant, resulting in the creation of lots of recipes that you can use."}, {"type": "example", "content": "A couple people are away this weekend and as a result I'm working all weekend."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Unlikely Conditional"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use conditional sentences to talk about events or situations that are unreal in the present and unlikely in the future."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If I had to live on what's in the fridge now, I would waste away to nothing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Depending on the context, you can express conditions that are not real or impossible in the present and not likely to happen in the future. <br /> Since these situations are not real, you have to remember the truth of the situation to use the opposite form of the verb."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">If I liked</span>  dogs, I <span class=\"strong\">would have</span>  a dog as a pet. <br />  <span class=\"strong\">I would have</span> a dog as a pet <span class=\"strong\">if I liked</span>  dogs. </span></span>  <br />  (the truth in the present: I don't like dogs. I don't have a dog as a pet.)"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">If </span> the president<span class=\"strong\"> weren't</span> so handsome, many women <span class=\"strong\">would not watch</span> the news. <br />  Many women<span class=\"strong\"> would not watch</span> the news<span class=\"strong\"> if</span> the president <span class=\"strong\">weren't</span> so handsome. <br /> </span> (the truth in the present: The president is handsome. Many women watch the news.)"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">If I won</span> a million dollars, <span class=\"strong\"> I would travel</span> around the world. <br />  <span class=\"strong\">I would travel</span> around the world<span class=\"strong\"> if I won</span> a million dollars.</span> <br />  (I think it is unlikely in the future that I will win a million dollars and travel around the world.)"}, {"type": "text", "content": "The structure for this second conditional is: <br />   <span class=\"strong\">If + simple past, would + base form of verb<br />  \u2026would + base form of verb + if + simple past</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "If there were more demand, I would open a small vegan restaurant."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If I could cook, I would open my own restaurant."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If I weren't so busy, I'd come and cook with you."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If I lost some weight, it would probably make her happy! "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Imagine that a vegan friend is coming to your house for dinner."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Plan a menu of at least 3 dishes that your friend can eat."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a list of all the ingredients. Look up any ingredients that you don't know in your dictionary."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Exchange your menu with another student and discuss which menu sounds more delicious."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I plan a menu for a vegan dinner."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I make a list of vegan ingredients."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I look up ingredients that I don't know in the dictionary."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I exchange menus with a partner and discuss which menu is more delicious."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"questions": [], "img_path": "", "stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about beliefs and opinions and use colloquial expressions."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about the results of an action or an event."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can write about unlikely or impossible situations in the present or in future."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What foods could you cut out of your diet to make it healthier?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "How difficult is it for you to make changes to your diet?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct"}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": " Making a big change!"}], "id": 0}, {"questions": [{"_data": [{"c